## Known Bugs
From our testing, we do not believe there are any major bugs still present, there may be a few small bugs we are unaware of but nothing we have found to be present within anything more than potential edge cases. 

Two bugs that we fixed:
In merge() while loop that go through specific range of array, it does not go through each element of the element in the range
When cutoff gets bigger, pthread_create might failed

Unpresent bugs:
When there are too many function calls for parallel_mergesort(), the number of args may increase which causes memory shortage, further causing error. During testing, we never reached that issue.  

## Reflection and Self Assessment

Aden:
Throughout our development, we didn't run into a major amount of bugs. Different group members had different 
understandings of Data Structures and Algorithms and Operating systems and we used these understandings to our 
advantage in the development of this project.  For me, my biggest lapse in understanding was the merge sort and 
how it works, since i havent done DSA as a subject yet, therefore, in my research, i used sources from 
GeeksforGeeks about merge sorts and merge sorts using multithreading. These sources helped my understanding of 
